# Agent 2 Testing Rules

## Deterministic behavior

Every test must be deterministic: no reliance on wall-clock time, random
seeds, network access, or execution order. Given the same input contract,
any Agent 2 function must produce the same output every time.

## Immutable contracts where practical

Every domain contract type (`app/agent2/types.py`) must be a frozen
dataclass, and its own test file must assert that construction rejects a
post-construction mutation attempt (`dataclasses.FrozenInstanceError`).

## Versioned policies

Any heuristic rule set (e.g. a future boundary-assessment policy) must be
tested against its own declared version constant
(`BOUNDARY_POLICY_VERSION` or a successor). A test must never assume "the
current policy" without pinning the version it is testing against.

## Tests for scope boundaries

`tests/agent2/test_contracts.py` (or its successors) must keep verifying,
structurally (via `ast`, not naive substring search over prose):

- no Tellurium/COPASI/`libsbml`/`libroadrunner`/`antimony` import anywhere
  in `app/`,
- no Agent 1 runtime/connector import anywhere in `app/`,
- no simulation, parameter-fitting/calibration, or model-critic function
  or class definition anywhere in `app/`,
- no Antimony-generation *service* module exists until an increment
  specification explicitly authorizes one.

## No hidden Agent 1/3/4/5 dependencies

A test must never construct or rely on a real Agent 1 database, ORM
object, or connector. Build test fixtures directly from
`app.agent2.types` (e.g. `Agent1CuratedKnowledgeViewContract` and its
nested `Curated*` records).

## No runtime network calls in unit tests

No test in this repository may perform a real HTTP request, database
connection, or subprocess call. Everything Agent 2 tests today operates
on in-memory contract objects only.
